{
  "id": "p15",
  "title": "Sets",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "p15-l1",
      "title": "set of",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "A set holds a group of values, each either in or out: var vowels: set of char; vowels := ['a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'];",
        "in checks if a value is in the set: if c in vowels then … That replaces long chains of or.",
        "A set can hold ranges too: ['a'..'z', 'A'..'Z'] is all letters. Sets work with small ordinal values (0 to 255): chars, enumerations, small numbers."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "program Vowels;",
          "var",
          "  vowels: set of char;",
          "  s: string;",
          "  i, n: integer;",
          "begin",
          "  vowels := ['a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'];",
          "  s := 'turbo pascal';",
          "  n := 0;",
          "  for i := 1 to length(s) do",
          "    if s[i] in vowels then",
          "      n := n + 1;",
          "  writeln(n, ' vowels');",
          "  if '7' in ['0'..'9'] then",
          "    writeln('7 is a digit');",
          "end."
        ],
        "output": []
      },
      "exercises": [
